    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes.' Notice the word order: 'yes' comes first, and 'yes' finishes the sentence. Max answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я так рад.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am so glad.' Here 'I' sets up the idea, while 'glad' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тоже рада.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am also glad.' You'll hear 'I' all the time in the show, here connected with 'glad'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Теперь мы вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now we are together.' The key word here means 'now', which Max combines with 'we'. Then Vika replies.",
